word clearly", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"text": "", "_data": [{"content": "slow down your speech", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 2, "correct": 1}], "id": 2}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nHow to give a talk.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Listen to the audio. Select the correct answer.\n", "type": "text"}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10re6aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}], "type": "DMC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 10, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "type": "RSLT", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 11, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn11le15ob10re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nPlanning a book launch.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn11le15ob10re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: \t\tSo Kristi, what do you think? It seems to be going well, don't you think?\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: \t\tYes, I think so. I can't relax though until it is completely over and nothing else can go wrong.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: \t\tI'll get you a glass of wine.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: \t\tThanks Adam but I would like to wait until we leave. I need to keep my wits about me in order that I'm able to deal with any issues that come up.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn11le15ob10re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: \t\tI think you're home free now. The catering arrived right on time and the food is excellent. The kids loved those mini pizzas. The wine is excellent. I thought we needed more bottles but we have just enough. People wouldn't take more than one glass. I guess the parents can't drink much because they have their kids with them. More for the rest of us! I'll save a bottle for you.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: \t\tYou're still working. I might need your help again. By the way, thanks again for getting Thomas here on such short notice. I'm so impressed by how much he knows about social media and how kids use it. He's such an eloquent speaker too. I can't believe he just walked in here and addressed the crowd like that without preparing.", "id": 2, "time": "18000", "image": "engenn11le15ob10re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: \t\tWell, he's so passionate about it that it's easy for him to talk about it. When we lived together he would try to teach me about it but I was never as interested as he is. \u2026 Wow, look at the line-up now to buy a signed copy of the book! People are buying it now since the launch has made it look so great.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: \t\tYeah, isn't it great? I didn't expect so many people would buy it here at the launch.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: \t\tI think Thomas really got people thinking about the risks owing to exposure on social media and as a parent that's something you would want to act on right away, right?\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: \t\tYeah, you're right. They're buying the book so that they can keep abreast of something that's changed a lot.", "id": 3, "time": "57500", "image": "engenn11le15ob10re2img07.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le15ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le15ob10re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Next Step", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Everything Is Perfect", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "  Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.  Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Will and Would to Express Intention or Willingness", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Will </span> and<span class=\"strong\"> would</span>  are modals . You can use these modals to express willingness or intention. Willingness can be defined as the readiness to do something.Intention can be defined as an aim.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Will/ Won't</span><br/> You use <span class=\"strong\">will / won't </span> to express that someone is / is not  not  willing to do something in the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br><span class=\"italic\">Richard is a nice guy; he <span class=\"strong\">will</span>  always help you if you are in trouble.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Fernanda is mad at me; she <span class=\"strong\">will not (won't) </span>talk to me.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would/ Would not <br/> </span>You use<span class=\"strong\"> would / wouldn't </span> to express that someone was / was not  willing to do something in the past.  <br/> <br/>  For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">My grandpa was such a nice man; he <span class=\"strong\">would</span> always help people if they were in need. </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> My teacher always helped me with unknown words, but he<span class=\"strong\"> wouldn't </span> translate the whole text.</span><br/><br/>Read the examples from the text. Keep the context in mind as you do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'll get you a glass of wine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "People wouldn't take more than one glass.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll save a bottle for you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we lived together he would try to teach me about it but I was never as interested as he is.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll call you as soon as they arrive.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Reason Clauses Including so ... (that)", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can introduce result clauses using words and phrases such as <span class=\"strong\">so that</span>, <span class=\"strong\">in order that</span>, <span class=\"strong\">because</span>, <span class=\"strong\">since</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">owing to</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"strong\">in order that / so that </span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">in order that </span>and <span class=\"italic\">so that </span>to talk about the purpose of an action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br><span class=\"italic\">I need to keep my wits about me <span class=\"strong\">in order that</span> I'm able to deal with any issues that come up.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">They're buying the book <span class=\"strong\">so that</span> they can keep abreast of something that's changed a lot.</span><br/><br>The difference between those two clauses is that <span class=\"strong\">in order that </span>is more formal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"strong\">Because</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You answer the question<span class=\"italic\"> why</span>? with <span class=\"italic\">because</span>. It is the most common word used in conversation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br><span class=\"italic\">I guess the parents can't drink much <span class=\"strong\">because </span>they have their kids with them.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"strong\">Since / Owing to</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">since </span> or <span class=\"italic\">owing to</span> to introduce a reason that the listener already knows about.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br><span class=\"italic\">People are buying it now <span class=\"strong\">since </span> the launch made it look so great.</span><br><span class=\"italic\">People are buying it now  <span class=\"strong\">owing to </span>the launch making it look so great.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I need to keep my wits about me in order that I'm able to deal with any issues that come up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I guess the parents can't drink much because they have their kids with them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "People are buying it now since the launch made it look so great.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think Thomas really got people thinking about the risks owing to exposure on social media.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They're buying the book so that they can keep abreast of something that's changed a lot.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "keep my wits about me", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be ready to think and react quickly in a situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need to keep my wits about me in order that I'm able to deal with any issues that come up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about work and working conditions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eloquent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "using \u200blanguage to \u200bexpress \u200bideas \u200bclearly and beautifully  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: He's such an eloquent speaker too.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "impressed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling admiration and respect", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm so impressed by how much he knows about social media.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to address", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to speak formally to a person or group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't believe he just walked in here and addressed the crowd like that without preparing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "passionate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having strong feelings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, he's so passionate about it that it's easy for him to talk about it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep abreast of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "\u200bstay \u200binformed on", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They're buying the book so that they can keep abreast of something that's changed a lot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le15ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine you are organizing a book launch for a publishing company.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of the things you need to do. Example: Guest speaker, Organize caterer, send out invitations etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Contact a speaker for the event.  What do you want them to talk about? Write an e-mail to the speaker inviting them to talk at the event. Include a formal greeting, closing and subject line.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your list aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I make a list of things to organize for an event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write an e-mail to a guest speaker.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my list of things to organize to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}